---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Section from "@/components/Wrapper/Section.astro";
import SectionLabel from "@/components/Site/SectionLabel.astro";
import PixelLink from "@/components/Site/PixelLink.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Electric Sheep Limited handles personal data under the Data Protection (Jersey) Law 2018 and the GDPR."
>
  <Section containerClass="section-split reveal-block" paddingBottom="small">
    <SectionLabel highlight="Privacy policy." />
    <div class="policy-intro">
      <p class="statement">
        We collect as little as we can, and tell you plainly what that is.
      </p>
      <p class="policy-updated">
        Last updated <time datetime="2026-10-05">5 October 2026</time>
      </p>
      <p class="policy-lede">
        Electric Sheep Limited (“we”, “us”, or “our”) is committed to protecting
        the privacy and security of your personal data. This policy outlines how
        we handle your information in compliance with the Data Protection
        (Jersey) Law 2018 and the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  {
    /* Twelve literal clauses rather than a loop over a local array: the visual
      editor edits copy in place, and an array in the frontmatter would put this
      text out of its reach. */
  }
  <Section paddingTop="small" gap="0">
    <article class="policy-clause reveal-block">
      <h2 class="policy-heading">
        <span class="policy-number">01</span>
        <span>Data controller</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="policy-body">
        <p>
          Electric Sheep Limited is the “data controller” for the information
          collected via electricsheep.design.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Company name: Electric Sheep Limited</li>
          <li>
            Email: <a href="mailto:hello@electricsheep.design"
              >hello@electricsheep.design</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>Address: 10 Minden Street, St Helier, Jersey JE2 4WR</li>
          <li>Registration: 149505</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="policy-clause reveal-block">
      <h2 class="policy-heading">
        <span class="policy-number">02</span>
        <span>Personal information we collect</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="policy-body">
        <p>
          There is no form on this website. If you get in touch, you do it by
          email, and we collect:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Identity data:</strong> your name.</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Contact data:</strong> your email address, and any other contact
            details in your signature.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Communication data:</strong> anything you choose to include in
            your email or its attachments.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>When you visit the website, we also collect:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Technical data:</strong> your IP address, browser type, the page
            you asked for and the page that referred you. This is recorded automatically
            in the request logs of Vercel, our hosting provider, for security and
            site performance.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Usage data:</strong> only if you accept analytics cookies, the
            pages you visit, how long you stay, how you found us, and your approximate
            location and device type, collected by Google Analytics.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Advertising data:</strong> only if you accept marketing cookies,
            the pages you visit, collected by the Meta Pixel so we can measure our
            adverts on Facebook and Instagram.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not run a mailing list.</p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="policy-clause reveal-block">
      <h2 class="policy-heading">
        <span class="policy-number">03</span>
        <span>Lawful basis for processing</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="policy-body">
        <p>We process your data under the following legal bases:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Contractual necessity / pre-contractual steps:</strong> we process
            your name and email to respond to your specific request for a quote, service
            or information. This is a necessary step before potentially entering into
            a formal contract with you.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Legitimate interests:</strong> we process technical data and keep
            a record of enquiries to manage our business efficiently, respond to people
            who contact us, and keep the website secure.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Consent:</strong> we use analytics and marketing cookies only
            if you accept them, and you can withdraw that consent at any time from
            <a href="#cookie-settings">Cookie settings</a>.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="policy-clause reveal-block">
      <h2 class="policy-heading">
        <span class="policy-number">04</span>
        <span>How we use your information</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="policy-body">
        <p>We use your data strictly to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Respond to enquiries you send us.</li>
          <li>Provide information about our services that you ask for.</li>
          <li>Maintain a record of business correspondence.</li>
          <li>Keep the website secure and working properly.</li>
          <li>
            Understand how the website is used, if you accept analytics cookies.
          </li>
          <li>Measure our advertising, if you accept marketing cookies.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="policy-clause reveal-block">
      <h2 class="policy-heading">
        <span class="policy-number">05</span>
        <span>Storage, security and retention</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="policy-body">
        <p>
          Emails you send us are stored in Google Workspace. Website request
          logs are held by Vercel. Both providers are ISO/IEC 27001 certified.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Retention:</strong> we keep your personal data only for as long
            as we need it for the purposes we collected it for. Vercel deletes request
            logs automatically after a short period, and Google Analytics keeps usage
            data for no longer than 14 months.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Security:</strong> we use appropriate technical and organisational
            measures to prevent unauthorised access to, loss of, or disclosure of
            your data.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="policy-clause reveal-block">
      <h2 class="policy-heading">
        <span class="policy-number">06</span>
        <span>International data transfers</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="policy-body">
        <p>
          Vercel, Google and Meta are based in the United States, so your data
          may be transferred to and stored there. Vercel also serves this
          website from a global network, so your visit may be handled in a data
          centre near you.
        </p>
        <p>
          We make sure these transfers are protected by appropriate safeguards,
          such as Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) recognised by the JOIC or
          under UK or EU law. All three are also certified under the EU–US Data
          Privacy Framework. Together these give your data a level of protection
          equivalent to Jersey law.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="policy-clause reveal-block">
      <h2 class="policy-heading">
        <span class="policy-number">07</span>
        <span>Sharing your information</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="policy-body">
        <p>We do not sell or rent your data. We only share it with:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Service providers:</strong> Vercel (website hosting) and Google
            (email, through Google Workspace, and Google Analytics if you accept analytics
            cookies). They act as “data processors” and are contractually bound to
            protect your data.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Meta:</strong> if you accept marketing cookies, the Meta Pixel
            sends details of your visit to Meta Platforms, which uses them under the
            <a
              href="https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">Meta Privacy Policy</a
            >.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Legal obligations:</strong> where required by Jersey law or a
            regulatory body.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The map on our <a href="/contact">contact page</a> is embedded from Google
          Maps. When it loads, your browser connects to Google directly, and Google
          receives your IP address and browser details. Google decides how it uses
          that information, under the <a
            href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a
          >. We do not receive any of it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="policy-clause reveal-block">
      <h2 class="policy-heading">
        <span class="policy-number">08</span>
        <span>Data we process on behalf of clients</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="policy-body">
        <p>
          Where we build and maintain applications for clients, we act as a data
          processor. That processing is governed by a data processing agreement
          with each client and carried out on independently audited cloud
          infrastructure.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="policy-clause reveal-block" id="cookies">
      <h2 class="policy-heading">
        <span class="policy-number">09</span>
        <span>Cookies</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="policy-body">
        <p>
          Apart from one cookie that remembers your choice, we only set cookies
          you have accepted. Analytics cookies (Google Analytics) and marketing
          cookies (the Meta Pixel) are off until you switch them on, and you can
          change your mind at any time from <a href="#cookie-settings"
            >Cookie settings</a
          >.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our <a href="/cookies">cookie policy</a> lists every cookie we use, what
          it does and how long it lasts.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="policy-clause reveal-block">
      <h2 class="policy-heading">
        <span class="policy-number">10</span>
        <span>Your statutory rights</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="policy-body">
        <p>
          Under the Data Protection (Jersey) Law 2018, you have the following
          rights:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Right of access:</strong> request a copy of the data we hold about
            you.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Right to rectification:</strong> ask us to correct inaccurate
            data.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Right to erasure (“right to be forgotten”):</strong> ask us to
            delete your data.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Right to withdraw consent:</strong> where we rely on consent,
            withdraw it at any time.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Right to object or restrict:</strong> object to processing based
            on legitimate interests.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Right to data portability:</strong> ask us to transfer your data
            to another service provider.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To exercise any of these rights, email <a
            href="mailto:hello@electricsheep.design"
            >hello@electricsheep.design</a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="policy-clause reveal-block">
      <h2 class="policy-heading">
        <span class="policy-number">11</span>
        <span>Complaints</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="policy-body">
        <p>
          If you are unhappy with how we handle your data, you have the right to
          lodge a complaint with the Jersey Office of the Information
          Commissioner (JOIC):
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Website: <a
              href="https://jerseyoic.org"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">jerseyoic.org</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            Address: 2nd Floor, 5 Castle Street, St Helier, Jersey JE2 3BT
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="policy-clause reveal-block">
      <h2 class="policy-heading">
        <span class="policy-number">12</span>
        <span>Changes to this policy</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="policy-body">
        <p>
          We may update this policy to reflect changes in the law or in how we
          work. The date at the top of this page shows when it last changed, and
          we encourage you to review it from time to time.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </Section>

  <Section containerClass="px-hover reveal-block gap-3" paddingTop="small">
    <PixelLink
      href="mailto:hello@electricsheep.design"
      color="var(--text)"
      fontSize={24}>Ask us about your data</PixelLink
    >
  </Section>
</Layout>

